{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1546439-my-father-died-today","id":1546439,"title":"My father died today...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-26T19:48:06-08:00","id":1546439,"title":"My father died today...","content":"...Well, today, one year ago, to be exact. <br /> <br /> He hadn't been doing well for a couple of years at that point. On complete bed care, unable to talk, legs and mind deteriorating quickly. Polite society says we're not supposed to say such things, but honestly, the man I had known and loved was already all but gone, I had mostly already made peace with that, and it was something of a mercy when his body finally gave out. It was my mother who I really felt bad for...After almost 60 years of marriage, she kept him home and took care of him as well as she was able, even cleaning and dressing him everyday until she finally was able to arrange for professional care people to come through daily. I helped out as much as I could...I'm just glad that I was spending the night there when it happened, I hate to think of her going through all of that alone...<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I was there, when she called me to their room because she could tell that something was wrong. We called the EMTs, who got there pretty quick, took one look at Dad and prompty announced that he was gone...I can still hear her screams when she heard that. All I could do was hold her...Then, as they were moving him out on the stretcher, they said there was life in him after all, so they put this breathing apparatus on him as they took him to the hospital. I rode along, as Mom couldn't pull herself together to do so. I sat in the waiting room, calling relatives, when they told me he was gone. <br /> <br /> There's a lot more, tho most of it is a blur now; getting back home and comforting Mom, my brother flying into town, tracking down the insurance info and getting on the phone to make sure the burial policy was still active, picking out a coffin, all three of us going to the funeral home to see his prepared body lying in state...I recorded most who spoke or sang at the funeral, but made the mistake of handing my phone to my Mom when I said some words, so she didn't get any of it! Just as well, perhaps, I'm not the greatest speaker. My last clear memory of that day is the coffin lowering into that deep hole in the Earth...The family came back to our house and ate and talked and laughed, but honestly I just wanted it all to be over...<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I was staying over again today, when Mom mentioned it was one year ago to this day; she's read some books on mourning, is getting out a little more now that she doesn't have to be around the house to care for him at all times, and her new cats keep her focused when she starts to feel lonely. She told me how much she still dreams of Dad, every night, and only rarely is he in that medical bed that we finally got rid of. No, he's his old self, walking, laughing, just the way we'd rather remember him. The pain will fade, but never fully die; neither will our memories, so long as we hold onto them, and keep them fresh and strong.<br /> <br /> I dunno, just wanted to share that. I know I haven't been around here for a while, or much of anywhere online, because of my own issues, health and otherwise...but maybe it's time to revisit my old stomping grounds again! <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T22:52:29-08:00","id":1546442,"title":"","content":"Thank you for sharing that.<br /> <br /> I live a pretty isolated life where I am here. I don't have much in the way of family, and most have moved away where it's harder to stay in contact with them. I was raised by my grandfather, and we're really all we have left for each other. He's doing very well for his age, but I see him slowing down, his balance failing here and there, and I worry, and I don't know what I will do. And I feel helpless.<br /> <br /> Mortality is a grim thing. I'm writing this to say I appreciate you sharing your reminiscence, and your observation of life going on, and the things we can still keep. I was in a place where reading that helped today.<br /> <br /> Everybody treasure who you've got while you still have them. I'll be trying my best as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T04:17:59-08:00","id":1546446,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing... I know it's rough dealing with the death of a parent. My Dad died 12 years ago and it's still hard to deal with sometimes...<br /> <br /> Glad you are there for your Mom though, it's important that y'all take care of each other.<br /> <br /> And if you need to talk or vent or whatever, we're all here for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T09:25:57-08:00","id":1546502,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys! It's good to feel seen, and I'm glad you got something out of this, too...Sorry I was late responding, Thanksgiving weekend at work took more out of me than I thought it would...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}